<article class="doc">
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
    {% include "partials/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
    <p class="micro">Support</p>
    <h1 class="doc-h">Something not working? Tell us.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>All Day I Dream About Sports is made by one developer, so the person
      who reads your email is the one who fixes the bug. No ticket queue, no
      bot.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Support%3A%20All%20Day%20I%20Dream%20About%20Sports">Email {{ site.email }}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{ site.issuesUrl }}/new">Report a bug on GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p>Replies usually arrive within a couple of days, in English. Mention
      your macOS version, your Mac model and, if it's a bug, the match and
      roughly when it happened.</p>

      <h2>Ways to reach us</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Email</b> - questions, bugs, feature requests and privacy
        questions: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</li>
        <li><b>GitHub issues</b> - bugs and feature requests are public, so you
        can follow a fix and see whether someone has already reported it:
        <a href="{{ site.issuesUrl }}">open issues</a>.</li>
        <li><b>The FAQ</b> - answers to the common questions on the
        <a href="/#faq">home page</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Alerts aren't showing up</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Check you follow the team - alerts only fire for teams you follow,
        and only while their match is live.</li>
        <li>Each event type has its own switch in settings. Make sure the ones
        you want (goal, card, full-time…) are on.</li>
        <li>With more than one display, check which screen is picked in
        settings - alerts and capsules appear only there.</li>
        <li>Alerts follow the live data feed, so a short delay after the real
        event is normal.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>My Mac doesn't have a notch</h2>
      <p>That's fine. On Macs and external displays without a notch, alerts
      drop from the top centre of the screen, just under the menu bar.</p>

      <h2>A pinned capsule is in the way</h2>
      <p>Drag it to any other corner - it snaps into place. You can also set
      capsules to small, medium or large in settings.</p>

      <h2>The app isn't running after a restart</h2>
      <p>Turn on <b>Open at login</b> in settings. The app lives in the menu
      bar and never appears in the Dock, so look for its icon at the top of
      your screen.</p>

      <h2>Privacy and your data</h2>
      <p>There are no accounts. Your teams and settings stay on your Mac; see
      the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for exactly what is
      collected.</p>

      <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
      <p>Just ask: email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
      or <a href="{{ site.issuesUrl }}/new">open a GitHub issue</a>. A person
      reads both.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
